= Secret Commonwealth Army Meeting

Through our intelligence work, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> has received a copy of minutes of a meeting between <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> leaders Garrick Crowde, Ulric Gorrick, and [? if not rohm_explode: Isen Glade?][? if rohm_explode: the leader of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>?], with former General Edwin Stallard, a close ally of Staal.

The topic of the conference was about possible joint action between the Commonwealth Army and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>, if the leftists were to make a move following the elections.

- @schleicher

@schleicher
title: Concerning.
on-arrival: staal_marcher_r -= 1; staal_marcher_support -= 1; royalist_urgency += 1; 

This all but confirms our suspicions about the "Red General." Staal is no <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span>—his god is order, not the Crown—but he is plainly preparing the army to move if the left rises, and he will make common cause with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>' paramilitaries to do it. Whether the rising he fears is real or imagined, a soldier who keeps one eye always on civil war is a soldier worth watching. Our relations with him have worsened.

- @schleicher_2

@schleicher_2
title: Staal offers to meet with the Free Guilds, and to ease their fears.
subtitle: The Free Guilds are independent of the party, and have agreed to participate.
on-arrival: staal_marcher_r += 1; staal_marcher_support += 1; labor_dissent += 5

The invitation for a direct meeting between Tobias Leighart, leader of the Greater Worker's Guild, and Staal is declined. Instead, a larger meeting is held, including Goodryke, his Interior Minister, and the Greater Worker's Guild’s co-chairs.

At the meeting, the Free Guild leaders confront Staal over alleged secret agreements with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>, prompting both Staal and Goodryke to strike a more conciliatory tone in response to Free Guild complaints about unfair government treatment. Staal denies any such deals with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>, insisting that the government's highest priority is reducing unemployment. Goodryke also requests the Free Guilds to use their influence to persuade the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> to give the government time to deliver results.

By the end of the meeting, the three unionists are left impressed by Staal, who hints at possible concessions to a “patriotic labor movement.” A line of communication between the Greater Worker's Guild and the government remains open—much to Vesh’s frustration, as he aims to maintain a united front against the regime.

(Leighart is granted an ability)